  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to normal\nretirement age for police/fire members of the New York city fire department\npension fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S4727",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4727-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 23,
       "fullName": "Jessica Scarcella-Spanton",
       "imgName": "1329_Jessica_Scarcella-Spanton.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1512,
       "sessionMemberId": 2340,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "SCARCELLA-SPANTON"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§501 & 503, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4727\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nnormal retirement age for police/fire members of the New York city fire\ndepartment pension fund\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide a twenty-year service retirement benefit for Tier 3 plan\nmembers in the NYC Fire Department Pension Fund to align with Tier 2\nmembers who are receiving that benefit.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend subdivision 17 of Section 501 of the\nRetirement and Social Security Law, and subdivision d of Section 503 of\nthe Retirement and Social Security Law, to provide that members in the\nNew York City Fire Department Pension Fund will receive a service\nretirement benefit after 20 years of service, regardless of age, and\nfurther provides that the bill shall take effect immediately.\n\nSection 2 of the bill amends section 503 subdivision d of the Retirement\nand Social Security Law to provide that members in the New York City\nFire Department Pension Fund will receive a service retirement benefit\nafter 20 years of service, regardless of age, and further provides that\nthe bill shall take effect immediately.\n\nSection 3 is a notwithstanding section 13-379 of the administrative code\nclarification.\n\nSection 4 is the enactment clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe existing statute provides for a normal service retirement benefit\nfor Tier 3 plan members after serving twenty-two years of service.\nHowever, members of the NYC Fire Department Pension Fund in Tier 3 work\nalongside Tier 2 members who must only serve twenty years to receive the\nsame service retirement benefit.\n\nThis bill seeks to align the service retirement benefit for Tier 3\nmembers of the NYC Fire Department Pension Fund with their Tier 2 coun-\nterparts so that there is equity amongst Tier 3 and Tier 2 employees who\nwork in the same profession.\n\nThe current disparity in service retirement eligibility must be\naddressed by this legislation because it creates the same 20-year\nretirement benefit eligibility Tier 3 members within the NYC Department\nPension Fund as Tier 2 members within the same Fund. This measure would\nensure fairness amongst Tier 3 and Tier 2 employees in the same work-\nforce by creating a uniform normal service retirement benefit.\n\nThis legislative amendment would also improve the recruitment and\nretention of experienced employees by creating an incentive for our\ndedicated employees based upon equality under the retirement laws.\nThese statutory changes would demonstrate that we value the commitment\nof these employees regardless of when they were hired, and regardless of\ntheir age or tier classification, which will ensure the continued deliv-\nery of high-quality public service to our citizens.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024- S.8818 - REPORTED AND COMMITTED TO FINANCE\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n",
